---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { ISSUES_URL } from '../config';

const summary = [
  { title: 'No data shared', text: 'Nothing goes to other companies for ads, analytics or anything else.' },
  { title: 'Encrypted in transit', text: 'Every connection uses HTTPS or secure WebSockets.' },
  { title: 'No account needed', text: 'Play without signing up. No email, phone or Google sign-in.' },
  { title: 'Deletion on request', text: 'Ask on GitHub and your profile is removed from the server.' },
];

const rows = [
  { type: 'Name', example: 'Your in-game callsign', purpose: 'App functionality', required: 'Optional. A random callsign is used if you pick none.' },
  { type: 'Device or other IDs', example: 'A random player ID created on your device', purpose: 'App functionality', required: 'Required' },
  { type: 'App activity: other actions', example: 'XP, level, kills, deaths, wins, rounds and season points', purpose: 'App functionality', required: 'Required' },
  { type: 'App info and performance: other', example: 'Connection ping, shown to players in your room', purpose: 'App functionality', required: 'Required' },
];
---

<Doc
  title="Data Safety · THRUSTLINE"
  heading="Data safety"
  description="The data THRUSTLINE collects, why, whether it is shared, how it is protected and how to delete it, as declared on Google Play."
  updated="22 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page matches the Data safety section of THRUSTLINE on Google Play. The
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains each item in more detail.
  </p>

  <div class="summary">
    {summary.map((s) => (
      <div class="item">
        <strong>{s.title}</strong>
        <span>{s.text}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Data collected</h2>
  <p>All of it is used only to run the game. None of it is used for advertising, analytics or personalisation.</p>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data type</th><th>What it is</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Required</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => <tr><td>{r.type}</td><td>{r.example}</td><td>{r.purpose}</td><td>{r.required}</td></tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Data not collected</h2>
  <p>
    Location, real names, email addresses, phone numbers, contacts, photos, videos, audio, files, messages,
    browsing history, health, financial or payment information, installed apps, crash logs and the advertising ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Data shared</h2>
  <p>
    None. The game runs on SpacetimeDB Maincloud (Clockwork Labs), the game's website on Vercel and this website
    on Cloudflare. They process data only to deliver THRUSTLINE, which Google Play does not count as sharing.
  </p>

  <h2>Security practices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Data is encrypted in transit with HTTPS and secure WebSockets.</li>
    <li>The server validates every move, hit and pickup, so other players cannot change your data.</li>
    <li>The code that handles your data is open source and can be reviewed by anyone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Clear the game site's data in your browser, or in the Android app long-press the icon, open
    <em>Site settings</em> and clear the stored data. To remove your profile from the server as well,
    <a href={ISSUES_URL}>open an issue on GitHub</a> with your callsign and level.
  </p>

  <h2>Android app permissions</h2>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Permission</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Internet</td><td>To load and play the game.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Network state</td><td>To show an offline screen instead of an error when there is no connection.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Doc>

<style>
  .summary { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .item { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: rgba(14, 20, 44, 0.55); }
  .item strong { font: 400 19px/1.2 var(--display); color: var(--ink); }
  .item span { font-size: 15px; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .summary { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
